<title>THAILAND: Thailand okays rice-for-plane deal with Indonesia.</title>
<headline>Thailand okays rice-for-plane deal with Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The cabinet on Tuesday approved a counter trade deal whereby Thailand will sell 110,000 tonnes of rice to Indonesia and buy two Indonesian-made aircraft in return, a government official said.</p>
<p>The official told Reuters that Thailand would buy two CASA CN-235 aircraft made by Indonesia's state-owned Industri Pesawat Terbang Nusantara (IPTN) for 831.59 million baht (US$33.27 million).  </p>
<p>In return, Indonesia's logistics bureau (BULOG) will buy 110,000 tonnes of various grades of Thai rice for delivery between November and February.</p>
<p>The rice to be purchased by Indonesia under the deal comprises 20,000 tonnes of 10 percent glutinous rice at US$460 per tonne FOB Bangkok, 65,000 tonnes of 10-15 percent grade rice at $335-345 per tonne, and 25,000 of broken rice at $237 per tonne.</p>
<p>--Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
